  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Drinking water needs assessment and study visit</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project is a needs assessment and study visit for relevant stakeholders in Zimbabwe&apos;s drinking water sector. The needs assessment should identify the essential needs of the Zimbabwe National Water Authority (ZINWA), the Ministry of Water, the water companies and the municipalities when it comes to managing drinking water supply services in Zimbabwe, with a view of what the Netherlands could provide them in terms of knowledge, capacity building and management services.The needs assessment is expected to primarily identify software needs and provide guidance on legislation, organization, planning, preparation, tendering, management, training, and capacity building. Additionally, there may be a need for new hardware, such as water infrastructure, for which Dutch companies could potentially be involved in the future. It is important to note that even with the current infrastructure, there is significant room for improvement in the drinking water supply.The consultants should identify the key people who should go to the Netherlands for a study visit to decision makers or influentials from within this sector in Zimbabwe. They could also come up with recommendations on who to include in the visit programme from the Dutch side.</narrative>
  </description>
